Success rate: 40.14%
Given an array A with N elements , you need to find the sum all sub arrays of array A.

Input Format:
First line contains size of the array
Second line contains the elements of the array

Output Format:
Print the Sum of Subarray using Contribution technique.

Constraints:
1 ≤ N ≤ 10^3
1 ≤ A[i] ≤ 10^3

Sample test cases
Input
4
5 3 -1 8
Expected output
64

  T.C: O(N) , S.C: O(1)

import java.util.Scanner;
public class Main {

    static void SumOfSubArrays(int[] arr){
		int ans = 0;
		int occ = 0;
		for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
			occ = (i+1)*(arr.length-i);
			ans = ans + occ*(arr[i]);
		}
		System.out.println(ans);
	}
-------------------------------------------------------------
